{"sha":"65d1f19e7d525f388b9852baeffe13008a9cfc8a","node_id":"C_kwDOTDJ7sdoAKDY1ZDFmMTllN2Q1MjVmMzg4Yjk4NTJiYWVmZmUxMzAwOGE5Y2ZjOGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Scormave","email":"5045197+Scormave@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-01T21:55:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"Scormave","email":"5045197+Scormave@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-01T21:55:02Z"},"message":"feat: Merge duplicate records with merge_objects

merge_objects merges a duplicate into the record to keep, for people,
families, events, places, sources, citations, notes, media and
repositories. It posts to Gramps Web's POST /api/{type}/{keep}/merge/
{duplicate} (API 3.15 or newer), which runs Gramps' own merge in one
transaction: the duplicate's details and every link to it move to the
kept record, and the duplicate is deleted. A merged person keeps the
other name as an alternate name and its Gramps ID in a "Merged Gramps
ID" attribute. Merging people also merges a family with the same
partner unless mergeFamilies is false; merging families merges their
different fathers and mothers, keeping fatherHandle and motherHandle
when given, else the kept family's parent.

Spouses, and a parent with their child, are refused before the user is
asked, with the update_family step that comes first. Like delete_object
and undo_change, the tool asks the user through MCP elicitation; the
question names both records and says what the kept one keeps and
gains, and the merge is refused when either record changed while the
user was deciding. Gramps' refusals (409), a record deleted meanwhile,
missing permissions and servers older than API 3.15 get their own
messages. The reply gives both handles and Gramps IDs, the transaction
that undo_change takes to restore the duplicate, the other records the
same merge joined and deleted, and the next steps, such as merging the
two Birth events a person merge can leave.

PostActionAsync takes an optional JSON body for the merge options.
Unit tests cover the question, the refusals, the request bodies, the
parent choice, the error replies and read-only mode; integration tests
merge two people and undo it, refuse spouses, merge two families with
different fathers, and merge two notes. Tried on demo.grampsweb.org
(Gramps Web API 3.25.1): person, family and note merges, the spouse
and parent-child refusals, and undo, after which the test records were
removed. README, the site, the tool catalog, the API inventory, the
configuration and client guides, the architecture notes, the server
instructions, server.json, the MCPB manifest and the changelog
describe the tool; the catalog counts 34 tools.","tree":{"sha":"2924b2d13167960d73abdc78add164b8d121aa6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/git/trees/2924b2d13167960d73abdc78add164b8d121aa6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/git/commits/65d1f19e7d525f388b9852baeffe13008a9cfc8a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commits/65d1f19e7d525f388b9852baeffe13008a9cfc8a","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commit/65d1f19e7d525f388b9852baeffe13008a9cfc8a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commits/65d1f19e7d525f388b9852baeffe13008a9cfc8a/comments","author":{"login":"Scormave","id":5045197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDUxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5045197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"Scormave","id":5045197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDUxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5045197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave","followers_